  urldate = {2025-01-06},
  abstract = {Nine varieties and two breeding lines of sweet Lupinus angustifolius were cultivated under organic and conventional conditions in Northern Germany in growing seasons 2010, 2011 and 2012. The alkaloid content was signiicantly inluenced by the growing system and year and also by genotype. The variety `Vitabor' and the breeding line `Bo 083521AR' revealed a very low alkaloid content in all years and cropping systems, while `Sanabor', `Borlu' and `Boregine' had a higher content. In the years 2010-2012 signiicantly lower alkaloid contents (475 {$\mu$}g g-1) were found under organic conditions than under conventional conditions (615 {$\mu$}g g-1). The mean alkaloid level of all varieties and breeding lines in organic farming was highest in 2010 (640 {$\mu$}g g-1) and lowest in 2012 (364 {$\mu$}g g-1), depending on temperature during the seed illing period. Investigations on the yield of L. angustifolius revealed signiicant effects of the genotype, the year and the growing system.},
